Restow recovery ISO

This live system restores a Linux machine from its whole machine backup in
Restow onto new disks. It starts the recovery program on the first console
(restow-recover.service); the program asks for the address of the instance and
the recovery code that an administrator issued for the machine there.

  /usr/lib/restow-recovery/restow-agent   the recovery program (restow-agent recover)
  /usr/lib/restow-recovery/restic         the restic it reads the backups with
  /usr/lib/restow-recovery/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
                                          the licences of both programs
  FIRMWARE-LICENSES.txt (this folder)     the licences of the non-free firmware

Nothing in this image belongs to an instance: no address, no key, no
certificate, no token. SSH host keys are made when remote access is switched
on in the recovery program.

The build recipe of this image is free software under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later; the source code of every package in it is
offered as an attachment of the release this image belongs to.
